  "content": "# Bounded LRU Cache in Python Using `collections.OrderedDict`\n\n## Introduction\n\nA **Least Recently Used (LRU) cache** is a fixed-size data structure that evicts the least recently used item when the cache reaches capacity. It is widely used in databases, web browsers, and operating systems to optimize resource access.\n\nPython's `collections.OrderedDict` provides an efficient way to implement an LRU cache because it maintains insertion order and supports O(1) reordering via `move_to_end()`. This tutorial walks through a complete implementation, explains every design decision, covers edge cases, and provides rigorous testing.\n\n---\n\n## The Complete Implementation\n\n```python\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    \"\"\"\n    A bounded Least Recently Used cache with O(1) get and put operations.\n    \n    Args:\n        capacity (int): Maximum number of items the cache can hold. Must be >= 0.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        if capacity < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Capacity must be non-negative.\")\n        self.capacity = capacity\n        # OrderedDict maps key -> value and maintains insertion order.\n        # Most recently used items are at the END of the dict.\n        self._cache: OrderedDict = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key) -> object | None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieve the value associated with key.\n        \n        If key exists, it is marked as most recently used (moved to end).\n        If key does not exist, returns None.\n        \n        Time Complexity: O(1)\n        Space Complexity: O(1)\n        \"\"\"\n        if key not in self._cache:\n            return None\n        \n        # Move the accessed key to the end to mark it as most recently used\n        self._cache.move_to_end(key)\n        return self._cache[key]\n\n    def put(self, key, value) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Insert or update the key with the given value.\n        \n        - If key already exists, update its value and move it to the end.\n        - If key does not exist:\n            - If cache is at capacity, evict the least recently used item (first in OrderedDict).\n            - Insert the new key-value pair at the end.\n        \n        Time Complexity: O(1) amortized\n        Space Complexity: O(1)",
